{{also|compétent|compètent}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|competent}}, {{m|enm|conpetent}}, from {{bor|en|fro|competent}} (modern {{cog|fr|compétent}}), from {{der|en|la|competens|competens, competentem}}, present participle of {{m|la|competō||coincide, be equal to, be capable of}}. Compare {{cog|nl|competent||competent}}, {{cog|de|kompetent||competent}}, {{cog|da|kompetent||competent}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-competent.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒmpətənt/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having sufficient [[skill]], [[knowledge]], [[ability]], or [[qualifications]].
#: ''He is a '''competent''' skier and an expert snowboarder.''
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=I believe in that myself because it has been explained by '''competent''' men as the convolutions of the grey matter.| author={{w|James Joyce}}| title=''{{w|Ulysses}}''| year=1922}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=That as a '''competent''' keyless citizen he had proceeded energetically from the unknown to the known through the incertitude of the void.| author={{w|James Joyce}}| title=''{{w|Ulysses}}''| year=1922}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} Having [[jurisdiction]] or [[authority]] over a particular [[issue]] or [[question]].
#: ''For any disagreements arising from this contract, the '''competent''' court shall be the Springfield Circuit Court.''
#: ''judicial authority having '''competent''' jurisdiction''
# [[adequate|Adequate]] for the [[purpose]]
#* '''1662''', {{w|Henry More}}, ''{{wsource|An Antidote Against Atheism}}'', Book II, A Collection of Several Philosophical Writings of Dr. Henry More, [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page%3AA_Collection_of_Several_Philosophical_Writings_of_Dr._Henry_More.djvu/109 p. 67]:
#*: For if they [birds] had been ''Viviparous'', the burthen of their womb, if they had brought forth any '''competent''' number at a time, had been ſo big and heavy, that their wings would have failed them, and ſo every body would ''have had the wit to catch the Old one.''
# {{lb|en|biology|of a cell wall}} [[permeable|Permeable]] to [[foreign]] [[DNA]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} [[resistant|Resistant]] to [[deformation]] or [[flow]].

